From 1567af39575edab457410545c45e97f6425e8631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: drewano <drewano@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 01:32:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-msm: mask controller IRQs while runtime suspended

The SDCC apps clock on Qualcomm platforms is a shared RCG which gets
parked on an always-on safe source (bi_tcxo) by clk_rcg2_shared_disable()
instead of being gated, so the SDHCI controller remains powered and
clocked while the host is runtime suspended.

On AYN Odin 2 (SM8550, 8804000.sdhci, rootfs on SD), the controller
keeps signalling status events in that state. sdhci_irq() returns
IRQ_NONE early once host->runtime_suspended is set, so nothing ever acks
or masks the source and the GIC keeps dispatching the level IRQ:
measured bursts of 15-50 irq/s on CPU0 whenever the host is runtime
suspended (ftrace shows one sdhci_irq() call per counted IRQ), with
zero mmc errors and no mmc traffic. Each dispatch pokes CPU0 out of
deep idle and blocks RPMh AOSD/CXSD entry during s2idle
(armada-os/armada#274).

Mask the normal interrupt enables in runtime_suspend, keeping only
SDHCI_INT_CARD_INT (SDIO wake) in case it was claimed, and restore them
from the untouched in-memory host->ier in runtime_resume. Boards using
a gpio card-detect (like Odin 2) keep hotplug detection; boards relying
on the controller-internal card detect keep it whenever the host is
runtime active.

Reference: armada-os/armada#274 (symptom 2), analysis of Pocknix 0210
(delayed clk-gating work, different SoC family approach).
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
index 0882ce7..9030643 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
@@ -2940,8 +2940,28 @@ static int sdhci_msm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&host->lock, flags);
 	host->runtime_suspended = true;
+	/*
+	 * The SDCC apps clock is a shared RCG that gets parked on an
+	 * always-on safe source (bi_tcxo) at clk_disable() time instead of
+	 * being gated, so the controller stays powered and clocked while
+	 * the host is runtime suspended and keeps signalling status events
+	 * (measured on Odin 2/SM8550: bursts of 15-50 irq/s on CPU0 with
+	 * zero mmc errors whenever the host is suspended, keeping CPU0 out
+	 * of deep idle and RPMh out of AOSD/CXSD - armada#274).
+	 *
+	 * sdhci_irq() bails out early with IRQ_NONE once runtime_suspended
+	 * is set, so nothing acks or masks the source while the line keeps
+	 * asserting. Mask the interrupt enables here, keeping only
+	 * SDHCI_INT_CARD_INT (SDIO wake) in case it was claimed, and
+	 * restore them from host->ier on runtime resume. Hotplug keeps
+	 * working through the external cd-gpio.
+	 */
+	sdhci_writel(host, host->ier & SDHCI_INT_CARD_INT, SDHCI_SIGNAL_ENABLE);
+	sdhci_writel(host, host->ier & SDHCI_INT_CARD_INT, SDHCI_INT_ENABLE);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&host->lock, flags);
 
+	synchronize_hardirq(host->irq);
+
 	/* Drop the performance vote */
 	dev_pm_opp_set_rate(dev, 0);
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(ARRAY_SIZE(msm_host->bulk_clks),
@@ -2979,6 +2999,8 @@ static int sdhci_msm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 		return ret;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&host->lock, flags);
+	sdhci_writel(host, host->ier, SDHCI_SIGNAL_ENABLE);
+	sdhci_writel(host, host->ier, SDHCI_INT_ENABLE);
 	host->runtime_suspended = false;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&host->lock, flags);
 
-- 
2.50.1 (Apple Git-155)

